Q) Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock

You are given an array prices where prices[i] is the price of a given stock on the ith day.
You want to maximize your profit by choosing a single day to buy one stock and choosing a different day in the future to sell that stock.
Return the maximum profit you can achieve from this transaction. If you cannot achieve any profit, return 0.

Explanantion:m
You don’t need to find the global min first.
l=0 (current day), r=1 (the next day)
Instead, as you iterate:
  check if the next day prices is more than previous days
  then calculate potential profit = current price - min price
  Keep track of the maximum profit so far

  else -> set l to r(the day we just said no to)

class Solution {
    public int maxProfit(int[] prices) {
        int max=0;
        int l=0;int r=1;

        int n=prices.length;

        while(r<n){
            if((prices[r]>prices[l])){
                int profit= prices[r]-prices[l];
                max=Math.max(profit,max);
            }
            else{
                l=r;
            }
            r++;
        }
        return max;
    }
}
